<article class="env-lemma" id="0BFC">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0BFC">Lemma <span data-tag="0BFC">39.9.4</span>.</a> Let $k$ be a field. Let $A$ be an abelian variety over $k$. Then $A$ is smooth over $k$. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      If $k$ is perfect then this follows from Lemma <a href="/tag/047N" data-tag="047N">39.8.2</a> (characteristic zero) and Lemma <a href="/tag/047P" data-tag="047P">39.8.4</a> (positive characteristic). We can reduce the general case to this case by descent for smoothness (Descent, Lemma <a href="/tag/02VL" data-tag="02VL">35.23.29</a>) and going to the perfect closure using Lemma <a href="/tag/0BFB" data-tag="0BFB">39.9.3</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>